content.text:
Now the big game.js. Let's write carefully. We'll implement full game.

Let me structure:

Constants:
FIELD_W=960, FIELD_H=540 (canvas size). Actually canvas 960x540. Use same.

Goal width 100, goal depth 20.

State global: mode, selected teams, match data.

We need UI overlays drawn on canvas or DOM? Simpler: draw everything on canvas including menus. But text input? no. We'll draw menus on canvas and handle clicks via mouse/touch coordinates. Also keyboard.

Let's implement canvas-based UI with clickable regions. Track mouse position and clicks.

Game states:
- 'menu'
- 'teamSelect' (choose human team and opponent)
- 'match'
- 'pause'
- 'result'
- 'story' maybe.

We'll implement exhibition: menu -> team select -> match -> result -> menu.

Let's write.

Player object:
{
 team, data (player data), idx,
 x,y, vx,vy,
 homeX,homeY,
 controlled:false,
 spirit, maxSpirit,
 hasBall:false,
 cooldown
}

Match:
{
 teamA, teamB, // team objects
 playersA[], playersB[],
 ball: {x,y,vx,vy,owner,ownerTeam, z?},
 scoreA, scoreB,
 time, half? , running,
 kickoffTeam,
 controlledTeam: 'A' or 'B' (human)
}

Let's set human controls team A always; opponent B AI. In team select, human picks team for A, opponent for B.

Formation positions: generate based on formation string. Let's create function getFormationPositions(formation, side) returning array of 11 {x,y} normalized 0..1. Side 'left' or 'right'. We'll define simple.

Let's implement formations:
GK at (0.05,0.5) for left.
DF line x=0.2 with y spread.
MF x=0.45
FW x=0.75
Adjust counts.

We'll write a generic formation parser: counts per line from string like '4-4-2' means DF4 MF4 FW2 plus GK. For left side. For right side mirror x=1-x.

Positions:
GK: (0.06,0.5)
For each line group, x = 0.2 + (lineIndex*0.2?) Let's do:
lines = [defenders, midfielders, forwards] with counts.
x positions: defenders 0.22, midfielders 0.45, forwards 0.72.
y positions evenly spaced between 0.15 and 0.85.

Good.

Now update loop.

Input handling: keys object. Also touch buttons set keys.

Let's code touch controls as DOM buttons that dispatch keydown/up by setting keys. We'll create in JS.

Let's write game.js in parts. First setup canvas, resize, input.

Let's draft.

We need to be careful with performance: update 60fps, draw all.

AI logic:
For each player in team B (AI) and also non-controlled teammates in team A.

We'll handle per player in updatePlayers(match, dt).

Pseudo:

function updateAI(p, team, opp, ball, isHumanTeam, controlled) {
  if (p === controlled) return; // human controlled handled separately
  // determine target
  let target = {x:p.homeX, y:p.homeY};
  const hasBallTeam = ball.ownerTeam === team.side; // 'A'/'B'
  // find nearest to ball among this team
  ...
  if (ball.ownerTeam === team.side) {
     // support
     if (p.data.pos === 'FW') target = {x: fieldW*0.75, y: p.homeY};
     else if (p.data.pos==='MF') target = {x: fieldW*0.5, y: p.homeY};
     else target = {x: p.homeX, y:p.homeY};
  } else if (ball.ownerTeam === opp.side) {
     // defense: nearest chase
     if (p === nearestDefender) target = {x: ball.x, y: ball.y};
     else target = {x: p.homeX, y:p.homeY};
  } else {
     // loose ball: nearest chase
     if (p === nearest) target = {x: ball.x, y: ball.y};
     else target = {x: p.homeX, y:p.homeY};
  }
  // move toward target
  const dx=target.x-p.x, dy=target.y-p.y;
  const dist=Math.hypot(dx,dy);
  if (dist>5){ p.vx = dx/dist * speed; p.vy=dy/dist*speed; }
  else { p.vx*=0.8; p.vy*=0.8; }
}

But for human controlled player, movement from keys.

Ball possession update:
- If ball.owner is a player, ball.x = player.x + (team side? offset); ball.y=player.y; ball.vx=0;ball.vy=0.
Offset: +18 in facing direction? We'll just center on player; okay. But shooting direction needs facing. Track player.facing angle. Controlled player facing from movement or toward opponent goal. We'll set facing based on velocity or default toward opponent goal.

- If no owner, integrate ball velocity with friction. Check collisions with players: if distance < 22, assign owner to nearest (with some cooldown). Also check goals.

Shooting/passing functions.

Let's implement input actions on key press (edge-triggered). We'll track prev keys to detect presses.

Actions:
- Pass: on Space press if controlled player has ball.
- Shoot: on KeyX if has ball.
- Tackle: on KeyZ if not has ball (attempt steal if near).
- Sprint: KeyC held sets sprint (speed boost) consumes spirit.

Special shot: if Shoot and spirit>=50 and player.special, trigger specialShot(player). Else normal shot.

Special shot visual: set state.special = {text, timer, player}. Ball speed higher and trail.

Let's code shot:
function shoot(player, special) {
  const teamSide = player.teamSide; // 'A'/'B'
  const oppGoalX = teamSide==='A' ? FIELD_W : 0;
  const goalY = FIELD_H/2;
  const dx = oppGoalX - player.x;
  const dy = goalY - player.y;
  const len = Math.hypot(dx,dy);
  // aim slightly based on player facing/movement
  let ax = dx/len, ay = dy/len;
  // add lateral aim from vertical input? keep simple.
  const power = (player.data.shot/10)* (special? 900 : 500) + 200;
  ball.owner=null; ball.ownerTeam=null; ball.ownerPlayer=null;
  ball.x=player.x; ball.y=player.y;
  ball.vx = ax*power/60? Let's use per-frame velocity. If 60fps, speed px/frame. Let's set ball.vx = ax*12; ball.vy=ay*12; for normal. Special: 18. Then friction 0.99.
  player.data... spirit reduce if special.
  if special: spirit -=50; specialEffect...
}

Pass:
function pass(player) {
  // find best teammate
  let best=null, bestScore=-Infinity;
  for p in teammates:
    if p===player continue;
    const dx=p.x-player.x, dy=p.y-player.y;
    const dist=Math.hypot(dx,dy);
    if (dist<30) continue;
    // prefer forward direction toward opponent goal
    const goalX = player.teamSide==='A'? FIELD_W:0;
    const forward = (goalX-player.x)>0? (p.x-player.x) : (player.x-p.x);
    const score = forward - dist*0.3;
    if (score>bestScore){bestScore=score;best=p;}
  if (!best) return;
  const dx=best.x-player.x, dy=best.y-player.y, len=Math.hypot(dx,dy);
  ball.owner=null;...
  ball.vx = dx/len*8; ball.vy=dy/len*8;
}

Tackle:
if controlled player near ball carrier opponent within 30, chance steal: if random < 0.4 + (def/20), transfer possession to controlled. Also knock ball loose.

Goalkeeper save:
In ball update when no owner and ball moving toward goal, if GK near goal line and distance to ball < 40, attempt save: if random < (gk.def/12) etc, set ball owner = GK, velocity stop, then after 0.5s throw. Simpler: GK catches and holds; on catch, reset to throw after timer. We'll implement GK possession then auto-pass forward after 1 sec.

Let's implement GK as player with pos GK. When GK gets ball, set a timer; after 1s, pass to nearest teammate forward.

Scoring detection:
if ball.x < -10 and within goal vertical (between goalY±goalHalf) => goal for team B.
if ball.x > FIELD_W+10 and within goal => goal for team A.
On goal: increment score, reset positions, kickoff to conceding? Standard: kickoff by conceding team. We'll reset with ball at center to conceding team's striker? Simpler: reset positions and set ball owner to center midfielder of conceding? Actually after goal, kickoff by team that conceded. We'll give ball to conceding team's MF at center.

Reset positions: reapply formation positions to all players, ball at center.

Timer: match duration 180s. When 0, end.

Let's code now. It's long but doable.

Let's also draw UI menus.

Menu state: options ['Exhibition', 'Story', 'Controls', 'Teams']. We'll draw buttons vertically. Click handling.

Team select: two columns? Human team list left, opponent right. Or select human then opponent sequentially. Simpler: first click human team, then opponent team. State 'teamSelect' with step 0 (choose human), 1 (choose opponent). Display teams list. Click team button.

Result state: show score, winner, button back to menu.

Story state: simple sequence of matches. We'll implement: storyIndex 0; show intro text; on click/enter start match with preset teams; after match, show result then next intro. Keep simple.

Let's code click regions stored as array of {x,y,w,h,action}.

Let's write.

For drawing text, use canvas.

Let's now write game.js.

