Calling doShoot directly works: ballX=869 owner=none. So the keyboard X press isn't triggering doShoot. Why? Because in updateMatch, edge('KeyX') maybe not detecting due to prevKeys sync issue. Let's inspect the edge handling code. In updateMatch:
```
const shootPress = edge('KeyX');
...
if (p.hasBall){
  if (shootPress) doShoot(p, m);
}
```
But `p` is controlledPlayer. controlledPlayer is Izawa. Should work. But maybe edge('KeyX') returns false because keys['KeyX'] is true but prevKeys['KeyX'] also true due to sync? Let's check: We sync prevKeys at end of loop after draw. But edge() function itself sets prevKeys[code]=cur when called:
```
function edge(code){ const cur=!!keys[code]; const prev=!!prevKeys[code]; prevKeys[code]=cur; return cur && !prev; }
```
So first time edge('KeyX') called when key pressed: prevKeys['KeyX'] from previous frame (false), returns true, sets prev true. Good. But we call edge('KeyX') in updateMatch. However updateMatch may be called multiple times? No. But the key press from playwright happens between frames; should be detected next frame. But maybe because the key is pressed and released quickly (playwright press), by the time updateMatch runs, keys['KeyX'] is false already! Playwright's `keyboard.press` dispatches keydown and keyup synchronously? Actually it may complete within one frame, so keys['KeyX'] true then false before update reads. That's why not detected. For manual play, user holds key long enough. For testing, use keydown, sleep, keyup. We did earlier with keydown ArrowRight and it worked. Let's test shoot with keydown KeyX, sleep, keyup.

